# This is an example file to show how to build the docker image for LumenWEB. You can either load it locally or push it to a remote registry.
# Edit & rename it, then run it with `bash scripts/build.sh`
# Building it locally using docker buildx (adapt and uncomment before use):

docker buildx build -t edited-lumenweb:latest ./src --load

# This will build the image as edited-lumenweb:latest and it will then proceed to extract the archive and load it to the local docker engine.

# Pushing to a remote registry for multi-node usage.
# The example bellow will build it using buildx and it will push it to the tagged registry.
# MAKE SURE YOU'RE LOGGED IN TO THE REGISTRY.

#docker buildx build -t amazing-registry.dev/cool-person/edited-lumenweb:latest ./src --push

# You can add something like `--platform linux/amd64,linux/arm64` to the command to build cross-architecture images.
